  clock: 2  # 78fa
  nonce: 78fa  # 78fa
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (overlaps WI-tabig).\nMechanism holds: _index_django_relations_in_file (py.py ~4772-4911) fills related_managers only from ForeignKey/M2M fields (related_name or <model>_set) and manager_names from manager constructors; no @property is read anywhere in _collect_django_relation_index (py.py:4604).\nLive repro (analyze_python, scratch fixture: Order with @property fees returning self.all_fees(manager='objects'); OrderFee.order = ForeignKey(Order, related_name=\"all_fees\")):\n  order.all_fees.filter(...) -> python:django.db.models:0-0:filter:unresolved (framework_dispatch=django_orm)\n  order.fees.filter(...)     -> python:external:0-0:filter:unresolved\nThe +32 pretix figure was NOT re-measured.\nUpdates:\n 1. DUPLICATE FAMILY: WI-tabig (P4, filed 09-07) is the same shape -- OrderPosition.checkins = @property returning self.all_checkins(manager='objects') -- and proposes the mechanism (property-getter return path via WI-gubar's _build_property_getter_index, one-return bound). This item (P2) carries the measured value. Propose fold one into the other (owner decides which survives).\n 2. The DjangoRelationIndex docstring (py.py:4366-4372, from 17da6af2e9) lists \"a @property that returns a QuerySet (pretix's OrderPosition.checkins)\" as a CORRECT miss under the refutation condition. A fix must amend that text, and should keep the item's own rule: adjudicate on the getter's return expression, never the name.\n 3. Side observation, not this item's claim: order.fees itself is emitted as a calls edge to python:external:0-0:fees:unresolved even though Order.fees is an in-repo property symbol (receiver_type_id=Order is stamped on the edge). Not investigated whether a property-getter edge is expected there."  # 78fa
